Error [jet.TypedLiteralInHeader]: The `{` of this typed literal is read as the start of the body
  --> tests/ui/typed_literal_in_condition.jet:5:12
    |
  5 |     if a > I32{0} -> print("pos")
    |            ^^^^^^
 Why: In an `if` or `loop` header, `{` opens the body, so `a > I32{0}` reads as `a > I32` followed by the body `{0}`
 Fix: Compare with a plain number, as in `if a > 0 ->`, or group the literal, as in `if a > (I32{0}) ->`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0637

